We can make our IOC container to keep Spring bean class object in different scopes

The spring bean scopes in 6x version are
1. singleton(Default)   -|----> In standalone apps we can keep the data in the following scopes   
2. prototype            -|      a) Block Scope b) method/local scopec c) instance scope d) class scope e)applicatio scope 

3. request               |
4. session               |----> In web Application of java we can keep data in the following scopes
5. application		     |      a) request b) session c) page d) application scope
6. websocket			 |

Note : webservices app (resful app) = web Application++


=> To specify the spring bean scope we use "scope" attribute of <bean> tag in xml  driven configurations(Not so imp)
          <bean id="wmg" scope="singleton" class="com.nit.sbeans.WishMessageGenerator">
          .....
          .....
          </bean>
          
=> To specify the spring bean scope we use @Scope annotation in annotation driven configurations (required)
      @Scope is class level, method level annotation ie it can be applied on the top of class and on the top of the method
      
      We generally use @scope annotation along with @Componenet annotation and along with @Bean annotation